<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>x500_gimbal_lidar_thermal</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author>
    <name>Leoncio Hermosillo</name>
    <email>lhermosillo@pheratech.com</email>
  </author>
  <description>
    x500 with the CGO3 gimbal carrying three payloads on the end-effector: the gimbal's
    own RGB camera, the down-looking lidar rangefinder, and model://thermal_cam.
    Airframe 4028_gz_x500_gimbal_lidar_thermal. Pair it with worlds/thermal_sar.sdf,
    which is the only world here that contains heat sources.

    The thermal core is co-boresighted with the RGB camera (zero parallax) but has a much
    narrower FOV, so it sees a centre crop. It is a nested include, so the sensor lives at
    thermal::thermal_camera_link and its topic carries an extra model/thermal level:
      /world/&lt;world&gt;/model/&lt;vehicle&gt;/model/thermal/link/thermal_camera_link/sensor/thermal_camera/image
    The link is deliberately NOT called camera_link — the gimbal owns that name, and DART
    names BodyNodes by unscoped leaf name, so sharing it causes a duplicate-name rename in
    the log even though SDF scoping keeps them distinct. See model.sdf.

    Note the thermal camera CANNOT be shielded from the airframe: thermal sensors ignore
    visibility_mask, so model://gimbal_invis's trick does not transfer.
  </description>
</model>
